{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Integral Domain.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Integral Domain.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"integral domain integral domain","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Integral Domain.md","fileName":"Integral Domain.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Integral Domain","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ring and Ideal Foundations]] · [[Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic","Commutative Ring","Zero Divisor","Field","Prime Ideal","Quotient Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Integral Domain.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Integral Domain.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"integral domain integral domain","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Integral Domain.md","fileName":"Integral Domain.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Integral Domain","heading":"Integral Domain","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An integral domain is a nonzero [[Commutative Ring]] in which a product can equal zero only when at least one factor is zero. Equivalently, it has no [[Zero Divisor]]s.\n\nEvery [[Field]] is an integral domain, but an integral domain need not make every nonzero element invertible. A proper ideal is a [[Prime Ideal]] exactly when the corresponding [[Quotient Ring]] is an integral domain.\n\nThe modern-algebra development uses the absence of zero divisors to prove cancellation and to constrain characteristic. It also proves that every finite integral domain is a field by turning multiplication by a nonzero element into a bijection.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic","Commutative Ring","Zero Divisor","Field","Prime Ideal","Quotient Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Integral Domain.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Integral Domain.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"integral domain integral domain","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Integral Domain.md","fileName":"Integral Domain.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Integral Domain","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic","Commutative Ring","Zero Divisor","Field","Prime Ideal","Quotient Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}